#ROOM
Vnum     40801
Name     Gate of Akar Kesh~
Sector   mountain~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Eight great rivers converge somewhere far below, their combined
roar audible even here at the monolith's base. Akar Kesh's gate is
carved directly into the stone, ancient beyond easy reckoning, and a
single stairway spirals upward into the dark.
~
#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    40802
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    40945
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40802
Name     The Great Stair~
Sector   mountain~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The stair winds upward for what feels like far longer than the
monolith's height should allow, worn smooth by countless feet across
countless years. Faint carvings mark the walls at intervals, too worn
now to read clearly.
~
#EXIT
Direction down~
ToRoom    40801
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    40803
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40803
Name     Council Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A wide, circular chamber crowns the stair, ringed with seats
enough for the full Je'daii Council. Light falls here from an opening
high overhead, the only illumination in a room otherwise built for
quiet deliberation.
~
#EXIT
Direction down~
ToRoom    40802
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40804
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    40805
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    40806
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    40807
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40802 1 40803
Reset M 0 40803 1 40803
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40804
Name     Hall of the Eight Rivers~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A long, quiet hall here holds eight small basins, each fed by a
thin channel of water said to be drawn from one of the great rivers
below. Initiates are taught to sit before each in turn, though few can
say exactly what the exercise is meant to teach.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    40803
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 40802 8 40804
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40805
Name     Shrine of Ashla~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Warm light fills this small shrine, gathered somehow from no
visible source. The air feels lighter here, easier to breathe, though
whether that's a physical property of the room or simply the mind's
own reaction is a question Akar Kesh leaves deliberately unanswered.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    40803
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40806
Name     Shrine of Bogan~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Shadow gathers naturally in this shrine, matching the Shrine of
Ashla's warmth with an equal and opposite weight. Akar Kesh teaches
that neither shrine is meant to be feared - only understood, and held
in balance with the other.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    40803
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40807
Name     Ketu's Sanctum~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Bare stone and a single low seat furnish this small sanctum,
set apart from the Council Chamber below. Ketu spends long hours here
alone, in a stillness few initiates are ever invited to share.
~
#EXIT
Direction down~
ToRoom    40803
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    40808
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40801 1 40807
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40808
Name     The Tho Yor Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The largest of the nine Tho Yor rests here, ancient beyond
memory, its hull dark and silent after millennia of dormancy. This is
the oldest structure on all of Tython - older, some say, than the
Order itself - and the reverent hush of the chambers below feels, if
anything, understated this close to it.
~
#EXIT
Direction down~
ToRoom    40807
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ENDAREA
